       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-09-21 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Five Dead, One Missing After Flash Flood Sweeps Kerala's Nilambur</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India</span> <span>#Kerala</span> <span>#Flash Flood</span> <span>#Disaster</span></div>
       <p>A sudden flash flood in Nilambur, Kerala, tragically claimed the lives of five individuals on Sunday evening, with search operations continuing for a missing woman. The unexpected surge of water caught visitors off guard, transforming a popular recreational area into a scene of disaster.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-21/five-dead-one-missing-after-flash-flood-sweeps-keralas-nilam.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The incident occurred as people had gathered along the riverbed and atop granite boulders, enjoying the natural surroundings. The rapid onset of the floodwaters swept away numerous individuals, leading to a frantic emergency response.</p><p>Local authorities and rescue teams immediately launched an extensive search and rescue mission. Efforts are focused on locating the sole remaining missing person, with teams navigating challenging terrain and strong currents in the affected areas.</p><p>The tragedy highlights the inherent dangers of unpredictable weather phenomena, especially in regions prone to sudden heavy rainfall. Community members and local officials are working together to support those affected and to ensure comprehensive search operations.</p><p>What to watch: The progress of the search operation for the missing woman and the official disaster relief efforts.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Article faithfully matches source summary with no invented claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
