     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-21 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Money Power Influences Elections, Says CJP's Dipke After ABVP's DUSU Sweep</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#DUSU Polls</span> <span>#ABVP</span> <span>#Student Elections</span> <span>#Money Power</span></div>
       <p>Following the recent sweep by the Akhil Bharatiya Vidyarthi Parishad (ABVP) in the Delhi University Students' Union (DUSU) polls, Abhijeet Dipke of the Citizens for Justice and Peace (CJP) has asserted that &quot;money power drives elections.&quot; This statement, reported by India Today, highlights a recurring concern about the influence of financial resources in student politics.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-21/money-power-influences-elections-says-cjps-dipke-after-abvps.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Dipke's comment comes in the wake of the DUSU election results, where the ABVP, the student wing of the RSS, secured a significant victory. Such observations about the role of money in elections are not new, particularly in high-profile student union contests that often mirror larger political battles. Critics frequently point to extensive campaigning, advertising, and resource mobilization as indicators of financial muscle.</p><p>The DUSU elections are often seen as a crucial platform for emerging political leaders and are closely watched by national political parties. Allegations or observations regarding the impact of &quot;money power&quot; raise questions about the fairness and level playing field for all contestants, especially those with limited financial backing.</p><p>While the summary does not provide specific details on how money power was allegedly exercised in the DUSU polls, Dipke's statement implies a perceived imbalance. Debates surrounding campaign finance and transparency in student elections remain pertinent, echoing broader national discussions on electoral reforms. The outcome of the DUSU polls, coupled with such critical commentary, draws attention to the dynamics of student politics.</p><p>What to watch: Ongoing discussions on campaign finance and transparency in student elections.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary with appropriate contextual elaboration, without introducing unbacked claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/dusu-polls-abvp-victory-abhijeet-dipke-money-power-campus-bias-ptag-2999230-2026-09-21?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="article/2026-09-21/money-power-influences-elections-says-cjps-dipke-after-abvps.html" data-title="Money Power Influences Elections, Says CJP's Dipke After ABVP's DUSU Sweep"><b>Share:</b>
