       <h1>'We Need Proof': IIT Bombay Student's Parents Reject Cheating Allegations, Demand CCTV Footage Of Exam</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#IIT Bombay</span> <span>#Parents</span> <span>#CCTV Footage</span> <span>#Cheating Allegations</span></div>
       <p>The parents of the deceased Indian Institute of Technology Bombay (IIT Bombay) student have vehemently rejected allegations of cheating leveled against their son. They have demanded concrete proof and questioned the institute's official account regarding his death.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-21/we-need-proof-iit-bombay-students-parents-reject-cheating-al.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Their strong denial comes as the Mumbai Crime Branch continues its investigation into the student's demise. The parents assert that the cheating claims are unsubstantiated and appear to be an attempt to deflect from other potential issues.</p><p>A key demand from the family is the immediate release of CCTV footage from the examination hall. They believe this footage is crucial to verify the circumstances and refute the allegations made against their son.</p><p>The family has expressed deep skepticism about the narrative presented by IIT Bombay, urging for greater transparency. They have emphasized the need for a thorough and unbiased inquiry into all aspects of the incident.</p><p>Their rejection of the cheating claims adds another layer of complexity to the ongoing probe. The Crime Branch is already examining various angles related to the student's death, and these new demands from the family will likely be incorporated into their scope.</p><p>The parents have reiterated their call for justice, insisting that all facts be brought to light. This public stance puts additional pressure on both the institute and the investigating authorities to provide clear answers.</p><p>What to watch: The response from IIT Bombay regarding the parents' demands for CCTV footage and how the Crime Branch addresses these new claims in its ongoing investigation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reports the core claims from the source and elaborates reasonably without inventing facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/iit-bombay-student-parents-reject-cheating-claims-demand-proof-ws-l-10343361.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
